{
  "title": "Neurofibromatosis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4054/neurofibromatosis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neurofibromatosis is an autosomal dominant disorder caused by a mutation in the NF1 gene that codes for the neurofibromin protein that typically presents with skin lesions, lower and upper extremity deformities, and spinal involvement.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with the NIH Consensus Development Conference Statement criteria with the presence of a combination of cafe-au-lait spots, neurofibromas, freckling in axillary/inguinal region, optic glioma, lisch nodules, and the presence of a 1st degree relative with NF-1.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment depends on presence and severity of forearm, lower extremity or spinal deformity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1:3,000 births for NF1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**extremity deformities**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**congenital anterolateral bowing and pseudoarthrosis of tibia/ fibula and forearm**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**hemihypertrophy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**spine involvement**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scoliosis & kyphosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "atlantoaxial instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "autosomal dominant (AD)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "mutation in NF1 gene on chromosome 17q11.2",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "codes for **neurofibromin protein**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**negatively** regulates **Ras** signaling pathway",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "neurofibromin deficiency leads to increased Ras activity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "affects **Ras-dependent MAPK activity** which is essential for osteoclast function and survival",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Selumetinib selectively inhibits MEK1/2, a critical kinase downstream of RAS",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurofibromatosis is the most common genetic disorder caused by a new mutation of a single gene",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**scoliosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterolateral** bowing of tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bowing of forearm bones with obliteration of medullary cavity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/ulnar_2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Bowing of forearm bones with obliteration of medullary cavity"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ulnar pseudoarthrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/ulnar_1.jpg",
                      "caption": "Ulnar pseudoarthrosis"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "radius pseudoarthrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/radius.jpg",
                      "caption": "Radius pseudoarthrosis"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**neoplasias**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diagnosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diagnostic criteria",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "according to the NIH Consensus Development Conference Statement (1987) the diagnostic criteria for NF-1 are met in an individual if two or more of the following are found",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "six or more café-au-lait macules over 5 mm in greatest diameter in prepubertal individuals and over 15 mm in postpubertal individuals.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "two or more neurofibromas of any type or one plexiform neurofibroma.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "freckling in the axillary or inguinal region.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "optic glioma.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "two or more Lisch nodules (iris hamartomas).",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "a distinctive osseous lesion such as sphenoid dysplasia or thinning of long bone cortex with or without pseudarthrosis.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "a first-degree relative (parent, sibling, or offspring) with NF-1 by the above criteria.is based on presence of both",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "NF1 (von Recklinghaussen disease)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NF2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with bilateral vestibular schwannomas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Segmental NF",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "features of NF1 but involving a single body segment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation General",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often presents with anterolateral bowing of tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/18A_moved.JPG",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often presents with radial bowing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/radial%20bowing.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows radial bowing"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "verrucous hyperplasia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hemihypertrophy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/hemihypertrophy%20-%20courtesy%20of%20Miller_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**cafe-au-lait spots**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/Cafe%20au%20lait%20-%20colorado_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "axillary freckling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "scoliosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterolateral bowing or pseudoarthrosis of tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dermal Plexiform-type neurofibroma may be seen",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Lisch nodules",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/lisch%20nodules.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows Lisch nodule"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "are benign pigmented hamartomas of the iris",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Neoplasias (Neurofibromatosis)",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neurofibromas (plexiform-type)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/plexiform%20neurofibroma%20-%20courtesy%20of%20Miller_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "is pathognomonic for NF1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "present in 4% of NF1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be dermal or in deep tissues",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often associated with limb overgrowth",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Inoperable tumors may be treated with selumetinib",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can undergo malignant transformation to neurofibrosarcoma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Wilms Tumor",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scoliosis (Neurofibromatosis)",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/scoliosis%20-%20courtesy%20of%20Miller_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "spine is most common site of skeletal involvement in **NF-1**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scoliosis is NOT associated with NF-2",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "can take two forms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "idiopathic-like form (nondystrophic)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "longer curve and treatment resembles that for idiopathic scoliosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**dystrophic form**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "curve is typically **thoracic kyphoscoliosis** with a **short segmented and sharp curve** with distorted ribs and vertebrae",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "usually recognized earlier than nondystrophic form",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "generally characterized by a sharp angular curve involving 4 to 6 vertebrae",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Imaging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radiographs show",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**vertebral scalloping**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**penciling of ribs** (penciling of 3 or more ribs is a poor prognostic finding and associated with **rapid curve progression**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**enlarged foramina**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "MRI",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "always obtain preoperative MRI to identify dural ectasia and **dumbbell lesion** (neurofibroma on nerve root)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "paraspinal masses are useful to distinguish from idiopathic scoliosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "observation vs. bracing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bracing is not effective for dystrophic form",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nondystrophic scoliosis in NF is treated like adolescent idiopathic scoliosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decompression, anterior spinal fusion (ASF) & posterior (PSF) with instrumentation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "dystrophic scoliosis",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "perform early in young children (< 7 yrs) with dystrophic curves",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "complications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "high rate of **pseudoarthrosis** with PSF alone (40%)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "pseudoarthrosis rate still high with ASF&PSF (10%)",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "some recommend augmenting the PSF with repeat iliac crest bone grafting 6 months after the primary surgery",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anterolateral Tibial Bowing (Neurofibromatosis)",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "epidemiology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterolateral bowing is often associated with neurofibromatosis (NF1)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/congenital%20pseudo.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "50% with anterolateral bowing have NF1",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "10% of NF1 have anterolateral bowing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathophysiology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may progress to pseudoarthrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/congenital%20pseudo.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "differentials for tibia bowing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**anteromedial**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "associated with **fibular hemimelia** and congenital loss of lateral rays of the foot",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posteromedial**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/posteromedial%20bowing.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/posteromedial%20bowing2.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually congenital due to",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "abnormal intrauterine positioning",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "dorsiflexed foot pressed against anterior tibia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "will develop **leg length discrepancy**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "associated with **calcaneovalgus** deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Imaging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "obtain AP and lateral of tib/fib",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/congenital%20pseudo.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bracing in total contact orthosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "bowing **without pseudoarthrosis or fracture** (goal is to prevent further bowing and fractures)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "spontaneous remodeling is not expected",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "osteotomy for bowing alone is contraindicated",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bone grafting with surgical fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "in bowing with **pseudoarthrosis or fracture**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "amputation with prosthesis fitting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "three failed surgical attempts",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Syme's often superior to BKA due to atrophic and scarred calf muscle in these patients",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Techniques",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**intramedullary nailing with bone grafting**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/IM%20nailing%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "resect pseudoarthrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "insert Charnley-Williams rod",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/charnley-williams.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "antegrade through resection site, then retrograde through the heel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/ante-retro.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "< 4 y.o., extend fixation to calcaneus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "5-10 y.o., extend fixation to talus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "2 yrs. postop, typically a 2nd surgery to push rod proximally to free the ankle joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**free fibular graft**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/Free%20fibula%20graft%20-%20courtesy%20Miller_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often need to take fibula from contralateral side because ilpsilateral fibula is not normal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Illizarov's external fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4054/images/iliz.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Studies show between 8-10 years of decreased life expectancy compared to general population",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "High incidence of malignancy and hypertension",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
